   "reply": "I added `Ledger.close(name)` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py`. It raises `ValueError` if the account's balance isn't zero. Otherwise it removes the account. The whole suite passes: 3 tests, including the new one.\n\nThe new test, `test_close_requires_zero_balance`, covers three things:\n- Closing a non-zero account raises `ValueError` and leaves the account in place.\n- Once the balance is back to zero, `close` succeeds.\n- After that, the account is gone.\n\nClosing a name that doesn't exist raises `KeyError`, not `ValueError`. That matches how `balance()` already behaves. I didn't add a test for that case.",
